    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All green. The full suite (the single `AcceptanceTest`) passes and everything compiles.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `Idempotency-Key` behavior for `POST /api/owners`: when a create repeats with an already-seen key, the originally created owner is returned with **200** instead of creating a duplicate.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Declared the optional `Idempotency-Key` header parameter and a `200` response on the `addOwner` operation. The `spring` generator (interface-only) regenerates `OwnersApi.addOwner` with a `@RequestHeader(value = \"Idempotency-Key\", required = false) String idempotencyKey` argument, keeping the contract documented and the header handling idiomatic rather than reached for via `HttpServletRequest`.\n\n2. **`rest/idempotency/IdempotentOwnerCreationStore.java`** (new) \u2014 A small `@Component` with a single responsibility: remember which owner id was created for a given key (`ConcurrentHashMap`, `findOwnerId` / `remember`).\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Injected the store and reworked `addOwner`:\n   - Extracted the existing validate/derive/persist body verbatim into a private `createOwner(...)` method so `addOwner` stays a thin orchestrator (no catch-all growth).\n   - `addOwner` now first calls `replayForIdempotencyKey(...)` \u2014 if the key was seen, it re-fetches and returns the original owner with `200 OK`; otherwise it creates, calls `rememberForIdempotencyKey(...)`, and returns `201 Created` with the `Location` header as before.\n\nThe idempotency short-circuit runs *before* the household/duplicate validation, so a repeat with the same body replays the original owner rather than being rejected as a duplicate. Keys with no/blank value simply fall through to normal creation.",
