    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of every validation and side-effect applied when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`. The endpoint is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` \u2192 `createOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`).\n\n## Validations (in execution order)\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Missing role \u2192 **403**.\n2. **Bean Validation on `OwnerFieldsDto`** (`@Valid @RequestBody`, runs during argument binding) \u2192 **400** on failure:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(\"^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$\")`, `@Size(1,30)`\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(...\\.?$)`, `@Size(1,30)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,20)`\n   - `title`: `@Size(max=10)`; `address`/`addressLine1`: `@Size(1,255)`; `addressLine2`/`email`: `@Size(max=255)`\n   - `postcode`: `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{4}$\")`\n3. **Required-field re-check** \u2014 `OwnerFieldsValidator.validateRequiredFields` (non-blank firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone; runs *after* address normalization to catch whitespace-only). \u2192 **400** `MissingOwnerFieldsException`.\n4. **Telephone** \u2014 `TelephoneNormalizer.normalize` (E.164 validity + national-number length). \u2192 **400** `InvalidTelephoneException`.\n5. **Email syntax** \u2014 `EmailNormalizer.normalize`. \u2192 **400** `InvalidEmailException`.\n6. **Disposable email domain** \u2014 `DisposableEmailDomainValidator` (blocklist). \u2192 **400** `DisposableEmailDomainException`.\n7. **Postcode/region** \u2014 `PostcodeValidator` (postcode must fall in the city's region range). \u2192 **400** `InvalidPostcodeException`.\n8. **Registration date not future** \u2014 `RegistrationDateValidator.validateNotFuture`. \u2192 **400** `FutureRegistrationDateException`.\n9. **Daily capacity** \u2014 `DailyRegistrationCapacityValidator` (\u2265100 registrations for the day). \u2192 **429** `DailyRegistrationLimitExceededException`.\n10. **Household duplicate** *(skipped if `sharesHousehold=true`)* \u2014 `HouseholdDuplicateValidator` (existing owner with same householdId). \u2192 **409** `DuplicateHouseholdException`.\n11. **City capacity** \u2014 `CityOwnerCapacityValidator` (\u226550 owners in the city). \u2192 **409** `CityOwnerCapacityExceededException`.\n12. **Entity-level constraints at persist** \u2014 `Owner` `@NotEmpty` (address/city/telephone), `@Pattern` E.164 (telephone), plus the `@PrePersist` callback.\n\n## Side-effects (in execution order)\n\nBefore the create logic:\n- **Idempotency replay** \u2014 if `Idempotency-Key` header matches a prior create, returns that owner with **200** and performs no further work.\n\nDuring `createOwner` (field mutations on the DTO/entity + reads):\n1. **Address normalization** \u2014 mutates `addressLine1`, `addressLine2`, and composes `address` (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST/RD/AVE).\n2. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** (MapStruct).\n3. **Telephone** rewritten to canonical E.164.\n4. **Email** lower-cased.\n5. **Registration date** defaulted to today if null, then rolled forward to next business day (`BusinessDayAdjuster`).\n6. **`householdId`** set (SHA-256 of last name + postcode).\n7. *(unless `sharesHousehold=true`)* **`possibleDuplicateOf`** set if a same-name/same-postcode/different-phone owner exists.\n8. **`namesakeCount`** set (count of same first+last name).\n9. **`householdSize`** set (household members + 1).\n10. **`customerCode`** generated (`REGION-HASH8`) and de-duplicated (appends `-2`, `-3`\u2026 on collision).\n11. **DB INSERT** \u2014 `em.persist(owner)` assigns id; `@PrePersist Owner.defaultRegistrationDate()` fires (idempotent here); empty `pets` cascade is a no-op.\n12. **`membershipNumber`** set post-insert (`customerCode-M<YY>`, fiscal year).\n13. **Audit log** \u2014 one INFO line written to the `\"AUDIT\"` logger.\n\nAfter `createOwner`:\n14. **Idempotency store write** \u2014 remembers key \u2192 owner id (only if header supplied).\n15. **Response enrichment** \u2014 DTO gets transient derived fields (displayName, membershipLevel, etc.) and, via `@AfterMapping`, a `bulkSignupWarning` flag (true when >80 registrations today).\n16. **`Location: /api/owners/{id}` header** set; **201 Created** returned.\n\nNote: many of these steps each trigger a full `findAllOwners()` read (daily counter, household duplicate, possible-duplicate detector, city counter, namesake counter, household-size counter, customer-code deduplicator, and the bulk-signup warning) \u2014 a significant read fan-out per creation."
